    "result_text": "Only one test class exists, and the full `./mvnw test` build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure gate for membership level 4 in `OwnerMapper.java` (a single file touched):\n\n- Added a small, self-contained helper `membershipTenured(Owner owner)` that returns true only when the registration date is more than 365 days in the past.\n- Changed `membershipLevel`'s single return line: a tenured owner gets the extra level (up to 4); an owner without tenure stays capped at 3.\n\nBecause a newly created owner's registration date defaults to today (zero tenure), `membershipTenured` is false, so the pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 email, +1 namesakeCount 0) top out at level 3 \u2014 never 4. Level 4 is only reachable once tenure exceeds 365 days, exactly as specified. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` passes and the full suite is green.\n\nStructural impact was kept low: one file, one changed method (only its return expression edited), and the new tenure logic isolated in a fresh cohesive method rather than inflating `membershipLevel`.",
